WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.496
- Sally sells seashells by the seashore.

00:00:03.496 --> 00:00:04.549
- Sally sells seashells by the seashore.

00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:08.382
- [All] Sally sells
seashells by the seashore.

00:00:10.618 --> 00:00:12.869
- Sally sells seashells by the seashore,

00:00:12.869 --> 00:00:15.202
and Sally was a real person.

00:00:17.563 --> 00:00:19.206
- [Narrator] This is Mary Anning.

00:00:19.206 --> 00:00:21.680
She sold rare invertebrate fossils

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.698
by the seashore.

00:00:23.698 --> 00:00:27.659
Born in 1799, Mary was
something exceptionally rare

00:00:27.659 --> 00:00:29.726
for a woman at the time, (thunder)

00:00:29.726 --> 00:00:31.139
possibly because as an infant,

00:00:31.139 --> 00:00:32.571
she was struck by lightning.

00:00:32.571 --> 00:00:34.347
No, she really was.

00:00:34.347 --> 00:00:36.080
(jaunty music)

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.797
She was a paleontologist, a
fossil hunter if you will.

00:00:39.797 --> 00:00:43.189
When she was 12, Mary dug
up a 200 million year old

00:00:43.189 --> 00:00:46.841
marine reptile, the
ichthyosaurus skeleton.

00:00:46.841 --> 00:00:49.363
Translation: she discovered
the first complete

00:00:49.363 --> 00:00:50.780
fish-lizard, ever.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:54.500
Throughout her life, she
discovered tons of fossils

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.403
and sold rare invertebrates here

00:00:56.403 --> 00:01:00.281
by the seashore of
England's Jurassic Coast.

00:01:00.281 --> 00:01:01.920
Unfortunately, Mary lived in a time

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.432
when men ruled the roost and many of them

00:01:04.432 --> 00:01:06.911
routinely took credit for her findings.

00:01:06.911 --> 00:01:08.083
But even though she might not have gotten

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:10.123
the kudos she deserved while alive,

00:01:10.123 --> 00:01:11.802
she has gone down in history

00:01:11.802 --> 00:01:15.361
as the greatest fossilist
the world ever knew.

00:01:15.361 --> 00:01:17.403
She was even selected as one of the three

00:01:17.403 --> 00:01:20.533
most important female
scientists in Britain

00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:22.093
and inspired a tongue twister that's one

00:01:22.093 --> 00:01:23.541
for the history books.

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:26.643
- Sally sells seashells by the seashore.

00:01:26.643 --> 00:01:28.660
- [Narrator] No, weren't you listening?

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.493
Mary sold fossils by the seashore.

00:01:32.578 --> 00:01:35.161
(jaunty music)

